WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:00.030
<b>Summary of previous episodes</b>

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:05.730
<i>Last time on </i>Frankenstein Family<i>:</i>

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:10.710
<i>Snow-niisan suddenly disappeared.</i>

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.230
<i>Apparently his monster form asserted itself,</i>

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.990
<i>and he started running around as 
a wolfman, totally out of control.</i>

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:21.450
<i>While on his rampage, 
he ran into Sumire-chan.</i>

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:25.460
<i>Realizing he was attacking Sumire-chan,</i>

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.190
<i>he seemed to recover his 
reason, and he ran away.</i>

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:33.290
<i>Sumire-chan ran after the seemingly 
suffering wolfman, not realizing who it was.</i>

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:37.100
<i>That's where she found my brother, 
collapsed in human form.</i>

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.140
<i>She's a very kind person, 
so she took care after him.</i>

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:48.380
<i>But the way she looked at him 
suggested she was in love with him.</i>

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:54.400
<i>I ended up seeing it, and I... I...</i>

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:23.210
<b>Frankenstein Family</b>

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:42.450
<b>#11: Scales</b>

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:56.490
There.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:59.670
Hey, Tanisu.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.070
It's too damn small.

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:24.220
I'm just grateful we have somewhere to live.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.080
The rent is high, too!

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:29.120
Where's our room?

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.390
Upstairs! Come on!

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.280
No way! Not happening!

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.780
Let's go!

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.000
Hold it!

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:47.050
Just be grateful we could 
get a home this quickly!

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:47.790
Shut up!

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:50.930
They're girls, and we're boys.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.760
But there's only one bed, right?

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.370
Yeah, yeah!

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:56.100
<i>That's</i> the problem?

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.520
Tanisu and I will sleep on the floor.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.970
You girls sleep on the bed.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.510
I don't mind.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:09.850
But won't you catch a cold 
if you sleep on the floor?

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.230
There's no decent furniture here!

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.450
I get it!

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.390
I'll work it out, so just hold on!

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:32.380
Wow, the city's so different! 
So many buildings!

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:37.170
No, Aisuri!

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:41.190
Tani-chan told you not to eat bugs!

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.050
Like I care! Butt out!

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:53.670
You okay?

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:56.200
The air here is bad.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:03.070
The city's so great! 
You can even see supercars!

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.320
That little brat!

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.070
Aisuri.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.770
We'll get used to it.

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:06.570
But...

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.860
Doesn't mama make the best pizza?

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:18.750
Thank you, darling!

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:23.470
Well? This is a nice big place, right?

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:26.090
We can all play here together!

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.930
Cool!

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:31.670
Such fresh air!

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:35.100
There are places with clean 
air in the city, too.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:43.150
Snow-niisan... Snow-niisan!

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.440
There's even more interesting 
things over here.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:46.090
Come on!

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:47.690
Don't run so fast!

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:52.970
How are your studies going?

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:54.660
Really fun!

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.670
Suishi-neesan!

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.130
A popsicle! Eat with us!

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:10.250
Eat it fast or it'll melt!

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:11.980
It's really tasty!

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.030
How is it?

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:17.270
It's good.

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.050
Didn't I tell you?

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:21.560
Even Suishi-neesan likes it!

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.280
Can I have another one?

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:26.650
Next time. Let's keep going.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.210
Huh?

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:32.810
Hey, Suishi-neesan!

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:33.870
We're going!

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:51.720
Kanisu?

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:56.180
You okay?

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:01.190
How's your brother?

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.880
How about your sisters?

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:09.140
Did you have a fight?

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:10.360
I don't know...

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:13.940
I felt the same way when 
my brother and I fought.

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:17.990
But if you just apologize properly, 
you can definitely make up!

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:20.920
It won't be that simple for me...

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:26.780
I'm like those adults I hate so much.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:30.190
I tricked you.

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:34.200
Even about my name... it's actually Tanisu.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:36.250
I'm sorry.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:44.620
No problem!

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:45.950
I forgive you!

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.970
That fast?

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:52.530
Well, you apologized!

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:55.820
Besides, we're friends, right?

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:57.450
Sumire-chan...

00:07:57.450 --> 00:08:01.300
So if you talk to them, they'll understand.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:04.840
But I don't even know where they went.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:07.130
I've been searching all day...

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:13.100
No matter what happens, someone will 
always be waiting for you at home.

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:14.520
You mean it?

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:20.600
Because you're family!

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:23.830
Yeah!

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:36.070
<i>Because you're family!</i>

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:38.210
Gimme more!

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:40.160
You'll ruin your digestion!

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:41.410
Shut up.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:45.820
Huh?

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:51.930
Tani-chan!

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:52.590
Tanisu.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:56.590
Tanisu.

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:02.100
Snow-niisan!

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:04.100
Tanisu.

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:06.650
You came back?

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:07.510
Yeah.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.140
<i>Someone will always be waiting for you.</i>

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:42.660
Dammit...

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:44.600
That place is our home.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.250
Why can't we go back?

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:48.830
Even if we went back, we couldn't stay!

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:50.260
I don't care!

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:54.070
I'm going back to my home 
some day, no matter what!

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:56.330
This is a key to the secret passage.

00:09:56.330 --> 00:09:58.070
Secret passage?

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:03.390
Mom and Dad probably accounted for 
something like this happening.

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:08.410
So they stuck this key with 
the documents they left me.

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:11.670
And written on the documents
 it was with was:

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:14.020
"If you ever really need it,

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:18.710
pass through the secret passage to 
our home's basement, and get ready."

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:20.890
So what'll we find there?

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:23.040
Will it let us go home?

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:24.940
I don't know.

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:28.880
But it's the last resort 
Mom and Dad left with us...

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:32.960
<i>I just don't think we should use it lightly.</i>

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:36.320
<i>I thought so... the key is gone.</i>

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:59.010
Um... could I rent a boat?

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:02.710
What's going on? Here...

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:06.520
Please! I need a boat that 
can withstand the storm!

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:09.170
I'm just an elementary school teacher.

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:11.530
Why would you think I'd have a boat?

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:16.060
Someone you know must have one.

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:20.850
First, if you run a 
secondhand shop like this,

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:26.190
there must be some kind of rich 
family on your collection route!

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:30.980
Second, most people on this island 
need to get around on the ocean.

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:35.890
If you're a teacher, you must know 
someone who works with boats.

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:37.070
Third...

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:46.760
I thought about it, and I think... 
you're the only one who can help me.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:50.550
You're quite an impressive child.

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:54.310
You seem to have amazing 
analytical abilities.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:12:00.650
So you also must realize that I won't send 
a child out on the ocean in this storm.

00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:05.950
But... I want to go find 
Snow-niisan and the others.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.100
Did something happen to your siblings?

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:09.620
We should call the police, then...

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:09.620
Wait!

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:14.490
There aren't many people 
I can trust right now.

00:12:14.490 --> 00:12:17.500
You're one of them. An important one.

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:23.050
If I'm such an important friend, 
then explain things to me.

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:26.110
What's going on with you guys?

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:31.870
I see. You don't have to tell me.

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:35.180
You must have some complicated 
circumstances anyway.

00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:42.090
It was my fault. I made them 
all feel responsible for it.

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:45.360
I've been really selfish.

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:51.370
Without Snow-niisan, Ashisu-neesan, 
Aisuri-neesan, and Suishi-neesan,

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:54.460
the place I live isn't really home!

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:56.920
So...

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.960
When you see them, 
give them a proper apology.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:03.400
That's some good advice 
from a teacher. Got it?

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:04.260
Yeah...

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:27.550
Wei, what are you doing here?

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:30.820
Jeez, what an unreliable guardian.

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:34.120
A child in your care is in bad shape, 
and you're all slack-jawed.

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:39.080
What happened?

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:41.460
Tanisu-kun, what happened?

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:46.570
Snow-niisan and the others got mad
 at me and ran away from home.

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:50.260
They all ran away?!

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:52.170
In this weather?!

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:57.240
Wh-What's going on?

00:13:57.780 --> 00:14:00.140
Please go home without me, Kuma-san.

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:03.450
I'll bring them back, I promise.

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:08.280
I can't exactly let you go by yourself.

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:10.950
Wei, take me along.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.200
That's what I like to hear.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:16.190
Sit down.

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:18.290
Okay...

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:21.580
Um, when was the last time 
you drove one of these?

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:23.620
How am I supposed to remember?

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:25.590
It can't be that different 
from a motorcycle!

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:28.050
Moving out!

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:32.760
I'm taking over.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:14.160
<b>Frankenstein Extras!</b>

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:09.320
<i>Frankenstein Extras!</i>

00:16:09.710 --> 00:16:14.160
<b>Kano x Akatsuki Rin Chat time!</b>

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:11.210
<i>It's Kano and...</i>

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:12.310
<i>...Akatsuki Rin's...</i>

00:16:12.310 --> 00:16:14.160
<i>Chat time!</i>

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:16.580
Yeah!

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:18.370
Woohoo! Yahoo!

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:19.600
It's been such a long time.

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:20.770
It really has.

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:24.190
I'm nervous about meeting like this.

00:16:24.190 --> 00:16:25.160
So am I.

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:27.130
Are you doing well?

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:29.500
I think so. How about you?

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:30.800
I'm doing great.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:33.680
You are? Give me some of your energy, then.

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:59.530
Falling Into Spring

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:59.530
Kano

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:44.160
She started out on video sharing sites, and has 
now performed multiple anime theme songs.

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:51.920
She's known for her voice that combines gentleness 
and strength, with a transparent quality to it.

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:59.530
She's released four singles and two albums so far.

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:22.520
Akatsuki Rin

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:09.400
In 2015, she got a spot in the grand prix 
from an audition of more than 3,000 people.

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:15.570
Her talent was recognized, and in March 2016 she
 had a major debut with "Wings of Determination."

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:22.520
She's been aggressive about doing overseas events
 too, and is getting major attention these days.

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:25.480
The opening is a real earworm, isn't it?

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:26.810
<b>Sings OP Theme, "Early Days" 
Akatsuki Rin</b>

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:26.810
Thank you.

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:28.750
I always end up humming it.

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:33.400
<b>Sings ED Theme, "Falling Into Spring"
Kano</b>

00:17:28.750 --> 00:17:31.100
It plays during the commercials 
too, so I hear it a lot.

00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:37.300
It feels nostalgic, and kind of intimate.

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:39.560
Does it? I'm glad to hear that.

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:46.660
I've been told my way of 
singing isn't very friendly.

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:51.930
But the theme is family, so I tried 
to put a certain kindness in it.

00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:53.730
I like that most.

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:55.400
Thank you very much.

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:58.070
I feel like, thank you for helping to elevate me.

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:05.770
When I heard "Falling Into Spring", I felt 
like it was a song overflowing with hope.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:06.810
Thank you.

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:10.090
Spring is when everything starts.

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:15.860
And your voice, Kano-san, is so sensitive.

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:20.280
It makes it a very "spring"-like song.

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:25.050
When people ask what my music is like,

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:26.840
it's hard to respond.

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:32.130
I always found myself sweating, trying 
to figure out a quality answer.

00:18:32.950 --> 00:18:36.620
Next time someone asks me that, 
I'll probably steal that.

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:40.590
<b>What was your impression 
when you first met?</b>

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:45.390
You felt very fluffy. It was 
just like I imagined you.

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:47.350
Is that okay? Did you read 
that off cue cards?

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:48.890
No, no, no.

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:50.410
You feel very feminine.

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:51.770
Oh? Thank you.

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:53.330
You have everything I lack, I think.

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:55.070
Why are you laughing?

00:18:56.040 --> 00:18:57.860
I really am jealous.

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:00.700
Thank you. I'm very envious of you, too.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:01.570
Oh, please.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:03.950
Don't say it so flatly.

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:13.590
I was born in China, actually, so 
I've known about you for a long time.

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:15.040
Thank you very much.

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:18.370
You were already famous when 
I was in middle school.

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:20.580
For "Hello/How Are You" and such.

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:23.050
The old Vocaloid song.

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:24.430
Old Vocaloid song?

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:30.110
It was really famous, and I heard it then.

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:33.980
I thought it was great. 
That you were so feminine.

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:36.800
In China, my name is read as "Lu Nai."

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:38.370
Yes.

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:41.940
I thought it was a funny reading, 
so that was exciting.

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:48.950
I only knew you from your 
songs and your photos.

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:56.300
So at the time I just knew you were a delicate
 beauty, with a mysterious air about you.

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:58.380
I never thought you'd smile so much.

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:01.130
You smile so much.

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:03.970
You're so open and talkative.

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:05.220
Thank you.

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:08.220
<b>We asked them this question, too!</b>

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:13.890
Who's your favorite<i> Frankenstein 
Family</i> character?

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:20.470
<b>Who's your favorite
 <i>Frankenstein Family</i> character?</b>

00:20:13.890 --> 00:20:14.920
Tanisu.

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:15.480
Tanisu.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:16.040
Tanisu.

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:16.650
Tanisu.

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:20.490
Of course, they're all very cute.

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:22.760
Puppy. The big brother.

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:25.130
He's very popular, but...

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:27.420
I do like him.

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:28.120
He's cute.

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:31.210
"My dog doesn't like thunder," he said.

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:33.250
Isn't that cute?

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:37.320
The most moving scene in the first episode.

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:40.210
This is what made me like him,

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:44.890
is the moment when Tanisu says he 
wants to become a normal family,

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:48.120
and gets angry.

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:52.550
And his sister says, "Why do 
we have to be normal?"

00:20:52.550 --> 00:20:55.130
Yes. That's a great scene.

00:20:55.130 --> 00:21:00.230
Yes. And that really awakened 
something inside of me.

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:03.110
That's a very impactful scene.

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:09.580
After I watched it, and 
I was thinking, "Wow."

00:21:10.050 --> 00:21:12.040
Then "Shotanisu. Shotanisu."

00:21:12.690 --> 00:21:16.400
They started talking about 
how much they love shotas.

00:21:12.890 --> 00:21:18.540
<b>I like pure shotas like Tanisu.</b>

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:18.540
I laughed so hard, of course...

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:20.840
I like shotas, too.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.030
Do you?

00:21:22.030 --> 00:21:24.170
They're very righteous.

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:25.720
Yes, they really are.

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:26.910
It's cute.

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:33.140
My personal preference isn't 
the usual cute shotas,

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:36.380
but the slightly twisted, tsundere type.

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:40.520
I have to say, that's the most 
excited I've seen you today.

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:41.610
Is it?

00:21:42.330 --> 00:21:43.610
Whisper whisper.

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:47.490
I like more fragile shotas.

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:48.830
The slightly sickly ones.

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:51.040
Isn't that great?

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:56.750
Are we under some curse that says 
we have to talk about shotas?

00:21:56.750 --> 00:22:00.670
No one can resist the appeal of shotas.

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:03.220
Shotanisu is the best.

00:22:03.220 --> 00:22:05.050
Yes, he's the best.

00:22:05.230 --> 00:22:08.050
<b>Then let's try to draw Shotanisu! 
(And compete to see who's better!)</b>

00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:11.760
I'm going to win. If I try, I'll win.

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:15.980
If we compete on ugliness, I think I'll win.

00:22:19.460 --> 00:22:20.680
What?

00:22:22.450 --> 00:22:24.940
How did it turn out this way?

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:28.390
I think I might be a good artist!

00:22:29.810 --> 00:22:35.450
I bet if I didn't tell you this was 
Tanisu, no one would recognize it.

00:22:35.450 --> 00:22:37.690
One, two, three!

00:22:39.350 --> 00:22:44.820
<b>Artist: Kano</b>

00:22:39.530 --> 00:22:41.160
So good!

00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:41.800
Really?

00:22:41.800 --> 00:22:43.150
Yeah, it's so good.

00:22:43.150 --> 00:22:44.820
It's really cute.

00:22:43.530 --> 00:22:44.820
How?

00:22:44.820 --> 00:22:47.050
This is what I can do.

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:48.960
<b>Artist: Akatsuki Rin</b>

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:48.960
Tanisu?          Snow?

00:22:47.050 --> 00:22:48.970
This is my...

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:50.300
It's a horse, right?

00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:54.200
But it's kind of fluffy, so it's a dog.

00:22:54.200 --> 00:22:55.610
Sorry, Yanai-san.

00:22:54.200 --> 00:22:57.640
<b>Sorry to (the creator) Yanai-san</b>

00:22:57.640 --> 00:23:00.280
They're cute. I want them as a keychain.

00:23:00.280 --> 00:23:02.090
Really? You'd buy that?

00:23:02.090 --> 00:23:03.770
For 200 yen?

00:23:03.770 --> 00:23:04.850
100 yen.

00:23:04.850 --> 00:23:08.410
100 yen. Okay, 100 yen. I'll work hard.

00:23:08.410 --> 00:23:09.950
I'll make them by hand.

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:12.810
<i>Snow-niisan.</i>

00:23:12.810 --> 00:23:14.530
<i>Aisuri-neesan.</i>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.030
<i>Ashisu-neesan.</i>

00:23:16.030 --> 00:23:17.410
<i>Suishi-neesan.</i>

00:23:18.370 --> 00:23:20.060
<i>I want you to come back.</i>

00:23:20.830 --> 00:23:24.790
<i>I'll do anything to get you back!</i>

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:26.800
<i>My brother!</i>

00:23:27.330 --> 00:23:28.520
<i>My sisters!</i>

00:23:29.090 --> 00:23:33.530
<i>We're... family, aren't we?</i>

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:38.380
<i>Next time: "Frankenstein Family".</i>

00:23:35.370 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>#12:  Frankenstein Family</b>
